Package: droidcam
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, v4l2loopback-dkms
Recommends: adb
Suggests: kdeconnect
Description: use a phone running the DroidCam app as the computer's webcam
 The Linux client of DroidCam by Dev47Apps. It connects to the DroidCam app on a phone, over Wi-Fi or by USB through adb,
 and writes the phone's picture (and, if asked, its sound) to a v4l2loopback virtual camera, which every program then sees
 as a webcam.
 .
 The phone app is Dev47Apps' own and comes from the phone's store; this package holds only the computer's side.
 .
 The package depends on Debian's v4l2loopback-dkms, not on the bundled module of the upstream archive. KDE Connect is
 not needed to find the phone.
